  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nA tertiary alcohol $H$ upon acid catalysed dehydration gives a product $I$. Ozonolysis of I leads to compounds $\\mathrm{J}$ and $\\mathrm{K}$. Compound $\\mathrm{J}$ upon reaction with\n$\\mathrm{KOH}$ gives benzyl alcohol and a compound $\\mathrm{L}$, where $\\mathrm{K}$ on reaction with $\\mathrm{KOH}$ gives only $M$.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/fVFs9cvA43gTq2sBJ-pL8aamUV9DPuXd2cFGNHT06I4.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nThe structures of compounds $J, K$ and $L$, respectively, are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YyDZH",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{PhCOCH}_3, \\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{COCH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{COO}^{-} \\mathrm{K}^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BUUzb",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{PhCHO}, \\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{CHO}$ and $\\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{COO}^{-} \\mathrm{K}^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VOaPN",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{PhCOCH}_3, \\mathrm{PhCH}_2 \\mathrm{CHO}$ and $\\mathrm{CH}_3 \\mathrm{COO}^{-} \\mathrm{K}^{+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AtXM4",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{PhCHO}, \\mathrm{PhCOCH}_3$ and $\\mathrm{PhCOO}^{-} \\mathrm{K}^{+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nJ=\\mathrm{PhCH}=\\mathrm{O} K=\\mathrm{PhCOCH}_3 \\quad L=\\mathrm{PhCOO}^{-} \\mathrm{K}^{+}\n$$",
